  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Motorola Solutions has recorded $302M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Motorola Solutions won 188 awards so far, with an average award size of $1.6M, and obligations are up 58.6% year over year. Motorola Solutions received steadily growing obligations across recent fiscal years: $158M in FY21, $107M in FY22, $119M in FY23, $172M in FY24, $191M in FY25, and $302M in FY26. Motorola Solutions' federal work concentrates with a few large buyers and a small set of NAICS markets. Motorola Solutions received $155M from the Department of Justice, $74.1M from the Department of Homeland Security, and $65.2M from the Department of Defense. Motorola Solutions' top markets by obligation are Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing at $145M, Engineering Services at $81.6M, and Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance at $52.4M. Motorola Solutions' current-year totals are partial, covering fiscal year to date, and award-value tables list total contract values rather than obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Motorola Solutions' largest federal customers?",
        "body": "The Department of Justice obligated $155M to Motorola Solutions in FY2026 to date. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $74.1M and the Department of Defense obligated $65.2M. The Departments of Veterans Affairs, the Treasury, and the Interior follow with $3.8M, $2.4M, and $1.3M respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What product and service markets drive Motorola Solutions' federal obligations?",
        "body": "Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing is the largest market at $145M. Engineering Services and Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance together account for $81.6M and $52.4M. Other notable markets include Other Computer Related Services at $7.3M and Computer Facilities Management Services at $7M."
      }
    ]
  },
